-- title:
--   Rigidity of 𝒪-algebra maps out of O^{nr}
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime number $r$, a commutative ring $\mathcal{O}$ and an element $\pi \in \mathcal{O}$ such that the quotient ring $\mathcal{O}/(\pi)$ has exactly $r$ elements and the image of $r$ in $\mathcal{O}$ lies in the ideal $(\pi)$. Let $Onr$ be a commutative $\mathcal{O}$-algebra such that the ideal of $Onr$ generated by the image of $\pi$ is prime, and such that every $x \in Onr$ satisfies a monic equation over $\mathcal{O}$ modulo $\pi$, i.e. there is a monic $P \in \mathcal{O}[X]$ with $P(x)$ in the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$. Let $C$ and $C_0$ be commutative $\mathcal{O}$-algebras with the image of $\pi$ in $C$ nilpotent, and let $p : C \to C_0$ be a homomorphism of $\mathcal{O}$-algebras whose kernel has square zero in the elementwise sense: $st = 0$ for all $s, t \in C$ with $p(s) = p(t) = 0$. Then any two $\mathcal{O}$-algebra homomorphisms $\psi, \psi' : Onr \to C$ with $\psi$ followed by $p$ equal to $\psi'$ followed by $p$ are equal.
--
--   This is the rigidity (unique-lifting) statement for maps out of an unramified coefficient ring: over a square-zero thickening an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra map from $Onr$ into a $\pi$-nilpotent algebra is determined by its reduction, the algebraic substitute for formal étaleness of $\mathcal{O} \to O^{\mathrm{nr}}$. It is used in the Čerednik–Drinfeld part of the development, in the proof that the edge chart morphism attached to a fine Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation is étale.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CerednikDrinfeld_Onr_algHom_eq_of_comp_eq_of_sq_zero.lean

